    "note": "Version read: Amended 2026-08-13 (Assembly 2026-08-24 and Senate 2026-08-25 votes on it; Senate's first vote 2026-05-27 was on the 2026-05-14 text). Struck: the requirement that importers include a copy of the certificate (failure to report now an infraction rather than a misdemeanor, via 31615(a)(3)); training date moved from July 1, 2028 to January 1, 2029; 'at least one hour of live shooting' replaced by 'live-fire shooting exercises'; the Section 31640.5 topic list rewritten. Section 28235 also amended (account cross-reference), not quoted."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 27560 (Penal Code): Commencing January 1, 2028, a personal firearm importer shall also certify to the department under penalty of perjury that they have obtained a valid firearm safety certificate pursuant to paragraph (3) of subdivision (a) of Section 31615 or that they qualify for an exemption to the firearm safety certificate requirement pursuant to Article 2 (commencing with Section 31610) or Article 3 (commencing with Section 31700) of Chapter 4 of Division 10.\nSection 31615 (Penal Code): (1) Purchase or receive any firearm, except an antique firearm, without a valid firearm safety certificate, except that in the case of a handgun, an unexpired handgun safety certificate may be used.\nSection 31615 (Penal Code): (2) Any person who violates paragraph (3) of subdivision (a) is guilty of an infraction.\nSection 31640.5 (Penal Code): (a) An applicant for a firearm safety certificate on or after January 1, 2029, shall have completed a training course within the prior year that meets all of the following conditions:\nSection 31640.5 (Penal Code): (1) The training shall be no less than four hours in length, including live-fire shooting exercises.\nSection 31640.5 (Penal Code): (4) The live-fire shooting exercises shall take place on a firing range and shall include a demonstration by the applicant of safe handling of firearms and basic firearm shooting proficiency.\nSection 31640.5 (Penal Code): (b) The training course requirement shall not apply to individuals with valid concealed carry weapons (CCW) permits or who have completed a training course for an initial or renewal CCW license pursuant to Section 26165 within the previous three years."
}